{"id":"ed2709dc7cd09e87","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-thm-martin-axiom.md","title":"Martin's Axiom","display":"thm-martin-axiom — Martin's Axiom","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-martin-axiom","aliases":["58-thm-martin-axiom","Martin's Axiom","MA"],"display":"thm-martin-axiom — Martin's Axiom","depends_on":["[[../batch18/58-df-martins-axiom]]","[[../batch11/58-df-cardinal]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-martin-axiom"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-martin-axiom</span><span>Martin's Axiom</span><span>MA</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-martin-axiom — Martin's Axiom"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b4f557645bc9a749\" href=\"?note=b4f557645bc9a749\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-martins-axiom\">../batch18/58-df-martins-axiom</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak c=2^{\\aleph_0}\">\\(\\mathfrak c=2^{\\aleph_0}\\)</span> (continuum cardinal)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span> (cardinal predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\\)</span> (the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-fragment of Martin's axiom from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MA}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MA}_S\\)</span> (full Martin axiom below the continuum, defined below)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}full\\text{-}martin\\text{-}axiom}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MA}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\kappa\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\kappa&lt;\\mathfrak c\n\\to\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\n\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}full\\text{-}martin\\text{-}axiom}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MA}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\kappa\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\kappa&lt;\\mathfrak c\n\\to\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\n\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}martin\\text{-}axiom}\\ \\vdash\\\n\\mathrm{MA}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\kappa\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\kappa&lt;\\mathfrak c\n\\to\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\n\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}martin\\text{-}axiom}\\ \\vdash\\\n\\mathrm{MA}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\kappa\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\kappa&lt;\\mathfrak c\n\\to\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\n\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The full axiom symbol is now explicitly defined from the fragments supplied by the dependency.</li>\n<li>MA is an additional forcing axiom, not a theorem of ZFC; the displayed equivalence is its standard formal statement.</li>\n<li>The density premise applies to every member of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal D\">\\(\\mathcal D\\)</span>, and the bound is strictly below the continuum.</li>\n<li>Relative to the consistency of ZFC, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MA}+\\neg\\mathrm{CH}\">\\(\\mathrm{MA}+\\neg\\mathrm{CH}\\)</span> is consistent.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch18/58-df-martins-axiom","status":"resolved","id":"b4f557645bc9a749","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-martins-axiom]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-cardinal]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathfrak c=2^{\\aleph_0}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MA}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}full\\text{-}martin\\text{-}axiom}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MA}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\kappa\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\kappa<\\mathfrak c\n\\to\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\n\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}martin\\text{-}axiom}\\ \\vdash\\\n\\mathrm{MA}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\kappa\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\kappa<\\mathfrak c\n\\to\\mathrm{MA}(\\kappa)\n\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathcal D","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MA}+\\neg\\mathrm{CH}","display":false}],"bytes":1455,"backlinks":[{"id":"8f12f393ab28c4e4","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MA}_S$ 使用 [[../batch01/58-thm-martin-axiom.md]] 的完整 Martin 公理；$\\mathrm{CH}$ 使用 [[../batch04/58-thm-continuum-hypothesis.md]] 的连续统假设。"},{"id":"da331f774e716a0a","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MA}_S$ 使用 [[../batch01/58-thm-martin-axiom.md]] 的完整 Martin 公理；$\\mathrm{CH}$ 使用 [[../batch04/58-thm-continuum-hypothesis.md]] 的连续统假设。"},{"id":"92a5267ae8b